  "summary": "Brighten your meal rotation with this colourful <b>Moroccan grain salad</b> filled with hearty chickpeas, toasted spices, and dried fruits. Tender pearl couscous is tossed with sweet dried apricots, toasted pine nuts, and crisp English cucumbers in a warm cumin and cinnamon dressing. Fresh mint and flat-leaf parsley supply herbal brightness, while lemon juice provides a crisp acidity that lifts the earthy grains. This fully vegetarian dish offers a satisfying blend of sweet and savory elements inspired by North African spice markets. Served chilled or at room temperature, it functions wonderfully as a light lunch or as a side dish for festive feasts. The chewy texture of large couscous pearls combines perfectly with crunchy cucumbers and soft legumes. Preparing the dressing while the couscous steams allows the warm grains to absorb all the spiced orange blossom and citrus accents fully. Delight your guests with this aromatic, jewel-toned salad that celebrates plant-based goodness.",
